.TH LIBMPQ__ARCHIVE_CREATE_MPQE 3 2026-09-04 "The MoPaQ archive library"
.SH NAME
libmpq__archive_create_mpqe \- create an MPQE-wrapped MPQ archive
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B
#include <libmpq/mpq.h>
.sp
.BI "int32_t libmpq__archive_create_mpqe("
.BI "        mpq_archive_s **" "archive,"
.BI "        const char     *" "path,"
.BI "        const uint8_t  *" "auth_code,"
.BI "        size_t          " "auth_code_size,"
.BI "        const mpq_archive_create_options_s *" "options"
.BI ");"
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Optional version-100 attributes work in both MPQ v1 and v2. Combine
LIBMPQ_ATTRIBUTE_CRC32,
LIBMPQ_ATTRIBUTE_FILETIME,
LIBMPQ_ATTRIBUTE_MD5, and
LIBMPQ_ATTRIBUTE_PATCH_BIT in options.attributes to select arrays.
Zero disables generation. Any nonzero combination creates one (attributes)
file and consumes one reserved slot. Unknown attribute bits are rejected.
Capacity includes the attributes entry
and listfile if enabled; the internal attributes name is reserved.
Finalization writes the listfile, attributes, then the completed tables.
Checksums cover source bytes before compression; FILETIME defaults to zero
and patch bits are zero. Use libmpq__writer_timestamp() on an active writer
for an explicit timestamp. Path addition never imports filesystem timestamps.
.PP
Creates a new MPQE stream containing an MPQ v1 or v2 archive. The caller
supplies at least 32 authentication-code bytes. The normal writer first
finalizes a private temporary MPQ, then encrypts it and atomically publishes
the result when
.BR libmpq__archive_close (3)
succeeds.
.PP
Compression defaults to STANDARD. Add
LIBMPQ_ARCHIVE_CREATE_COMPRESSION_EXTENDED to options.flags to select
EXTENDED. The policy affects writer validation only, not decoding.
.PP
Existing MPQE archives cannot be modified. Creation uses temporary plaintext
storage in the destination directory. That temporary file is owner-only; the
completed MPQE archive uses normal output permissions determined by the
caller's umask. Cleanup is best effort, so a crash can leave an owner-only
plaintext temporary file behind.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns zero on success or a negative LIBMPQ_ERROR_* code. Missing or short
authentication data returns LIBMPQ_ERROR_DECRYPT.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR libmpq__archive_attributes_flags (3),
.BR libmpq__file_attributes (3),
.BR libmpq__writer_timestamp (3),
.BR libmpq__archive_compression_allowed (3),
.BR libmpq__archive_create (3),
.BR libmpq__archive_open_mpqe (3),
.BR libmpq__archive_close (3)
